From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:40:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 52/52] compositor: shadow and outline Wayland windows that
 draw neither

Wayland clients that don't draw a shadow of their own, like Luft's apps
and windows with Kestrel's title bars, used to blend into whatever was
behind them, most of all dark windows over other dark windows. Paint
them a shadow from the shadow factory, as X11 windows get, and a thin
neutral line along the inside of their rounded edge that lightens dark
windows and darkens light ones.

A window counts when its corners are rounded and its buffer doesn't
reach past its frame, where a client would draw its own shadow. The
shadow is never painted under the window, so translucent and blurred
parts of it stay clear, and both go away with the rounded corners on
maximized, tiled and fullscreen windows. The default shadows grow a
little softer and wider for every window.
